# The build context is copied wholesale before anything runs, so everything large and
# rebuildable is excluded here. node_modules and .next in this directory came out of the
# Windows upload — they are the wrong platform for the image and are rebuilt inside it.
node_modules
.next
out
build
*.tsbuildinfo

# The upload archive itself: half a gigabyte that would be sent to the daemon every build.
*.tar

# Reference material, not source. Already excluded from tsconfig and from Next's file
# tracing; excluding it here keeps it out of the image entirely.
design_handoff_moneybot_tts

Dockerfile
.dockerignore
docker-compose.yaml
.git
.gitignore
.claude
CLAUDE.md
README.md
# Every .env, not just the .local ones. The Dockerfile's builder stage does `COPY . .`, so a
# .env sitting here would be inside the build context and `next build` would load it, which
# is both a config it should not be reading and a secret-shaped file in a layer. Runtime
# config arrives from compose `environment:` and NEXT_PUBLIC_BASE_PATH from a build arg, so
# nothing in the image needs these. .env.example is excluded too; it is documentation.
.env*
